<description>&lt;p&gt;Gunmen attacked villages in Nigeria, killing 24 civilians, while bandits in Niger State killed an immigration officer and burned his body, and similar bandit raids continued in Borgu LGA. A Christian humanitarian worker was slain in northwest Nigeria and a Niger lawyer was jailed for a social-media post about the army. Ex-militants in Akwa Ibom pledged support for President Tinubu’s re-election, and ECOWAS leaders met with the junta in a panel photo. The conflict produced 4,159 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Hindu&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Nation Newspaper&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMingFBVV95cUxNTDJlWmRtTEpEcUY4X2w2SW95dWg3S3lRQkdWand6d3Z1S21IZmJqZEhTclQ3cEpaQ0FXOFpJTGd3bzJlN1F0ZUI0eTdpeWQ2U2NiU1ViVWZFMTdweFZ1c2g5R2FCQzBGMzNkamx2SmFRM0V1VGM0MS1tNGszRnBrUzZyNFZMRzlMZEdUWlFWQjNQUkxVWThfZHRHcEpUZw?oc=5&quot;&gt;beninwebtv.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixAFBVV95cUxQREo3aEY1WkNLZ3RwQWw3Rnh0eUFLZTlzWFdTVEJYSzNNOUJXeGhMdHpmX1FfQ3dLQmZRam45bkl6ODJweDh5U053QVM3bUs2MVBKTVdLeHdkVF9EX2JjQTczUWh0ZzJ5eWJNMjhHTTNDSUhyeVp5enBEMDdxX3RaT0pneUNPZDhzcnlfMkxFdktkVGYyaXpDa29oYVBRRzJKT09nSzcydnhEbVZxdjhIT0tZa3Y1M2VaQ2d4N192TkVnWW1S?oc=5&quot;&gt;THISDAYLIVE&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimgFBVV95cUxOdzlHMXN5NlVmT2NwSFZRakZYMFh3VUd1aXdDS2JLMVBqR1dBOHA2ak1qRzFwZVlRaU85UDhzTzZOOWFpb2hzc1BWMzBwTXozT1pBZHRjMUJCS0xFVlNmeHlaRE1vSU93YVFESVlDa1hZSENuZDRTQ24wejRjWktveEIyOTgxQWRneTNjODlqWmZmR0ozdnpxbnpn?oc=5&quot;&gt;Christian News Network&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijAFBVV95cUxQYlJCZ1JmUGhjNkJVZE1jWjJFMFV6aUVxb2FtZlpMVnJFVDZNS2g0V3hOZ1JpaE5ldWJpZDdnV1RoN0lYaWE5THlfR